{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the wrath will turn back, etc.</b> It was necessary to turn back the wrath even after carrying out judgment, because a court of the lower court punishes only those who act with witnesses and warning, whereas if HaShem were to carry out judgment He would strike even those who act without witnesses and without warning, and when the destroyer goes forth he destroys also those who devise evil thoughts. Therefore He said to them to carry out judgment, and through this His wrath would turn back, so that He would not destroy those who committed the act without witnesses and without warning, etc., and they would turn back and live."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:14:08.264587508Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}